      },
      "text": "The history of science is the longest-standing and most developed subfield of intellectual\nhistory. It has its own professional discipline (History of Science Society, Isis journal, 1913)\nand has gone through multiple methodological revolutions — from hagiography and Whig history,\nthrough internalist-externalist debates, to contextual, sociological, and postcolonial approaches."
